Authorization Management System (AMS)
Final Product Definition
1. Purpose of AMS
Authorization Management System (AMS) is a web-based application designed to control and manage the complete lifecycle of personnel authorizations within the organization.
The system will replace manual authorization processing and provide a controlled digital workflow for:
•	Application submission
•	Document verification
•	Competency assessment
•	HQC approval
•	Authorization issuance
•	Certificate generation
•	Candidate acknowledgement
•	Renewal
•	Extension
•	Amendment
•	Loss/reissue
•	Withdrawal
•	Historical traceability
________________________________________
2. Final Outcome (The Actual Product)
The final product is not a document system.
The final product is:
A live authorization control portal used by candidates, Quality Department personnel, reviewers, and HQC to manage authorization privileges from application to expiry.
________________________________________
3. Users of AMS
3.1 Candidate / Auditor
The person requesting authorization.
Can:
•	Login
•	View profile
•	Create application
•	Upload documents
•	Track application status
•	View issued authorization
•	Download certificate
•	Read terms and conditions
•	Provide acknowledgement
Cannot:
•	Approve own application
•	Modify granted scope
•	Modify assessment
•	Issue certificate
________________________________________
3.2 QA Staff
Quality Department personnel.
Can:
•	View all applications
•	View authorization records
•	Manage workflow
•	Perform assigned activities based on capability
________________________________________
3.3 Delegated QA Reviewer
Can perform:
•	Document verification
Example:
Qualification review
Training review
Experience verification
Cannot:
•	Final approve authorization
________________________________________
3.4 Assessment Reviewer / Lead Auditor
Can perform:
•	Competency assessment
•	TMA/QA/GEN/12c digital checklist
•	Knowledge evaluation
•	Understanding evaluation
•	Ability evaluation
•	Practical assessment
Important:
The same person may perform:
Document Review + Assessment
if they have the required capability.
________________________________________
3.5 HQC
Head of Quality and Compliance.
Final authority.
Only HQC can:
•	Approve authorization
•	Reject authorization
•	Decide final scope
•	Decide limitations
•	Issue authorization
________________________________________
3.6 System Administrator
Controls:
•	User creation
•	Password reset
•	Capability assignment
•	System settings
________________________________________
